    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I feel like <code>Fin.predAbove</code> should have been defined differently. Instead of<br>\n<code>def predAbove (p : Fin n) (i : Fin (n + 1)) : Fin n</code><br>\nit should be<br>\n<code>def predAbove (p : Fin (n + 1)) (i : Fin (n + 1)) : Fin n</code><br>\nso that <code>p</code> could also be <code>Fin.last n</code>.</p>",
        "id": 584270574,
        "sender_full_name": "Bjørn Kjos-Hanssen",
        "timestamp": 1775666553
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There's only one surjection <code>Fin 2 -&gt; Fin 1</code> so it feels right that the surjections are indexed by <code>Fin 1</code>.</p>",
        "id": 584274688,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1775667819
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If p is <code>Fin.last n</code> then it's <code>n</code> so <code>p &lt; i</code> is never true so you want to map <code>n : Fin (n + 1)</code> to <code>n : Fin n</code> which doesn't look right in this context.</p>",
        "id": 584275212,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1775667977
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes there is actually a natural function you're describing, I looked into this a lot before. But it's kind of one of those pick your poison things</p>",
        "id": 584279105,
        "sender_full_name": "Wrenna Robson",
        "timestamp": 1775669251
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"330967\">Wrenna Robson</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/succAbove.20and.20predAbove.20lemmas/near/584279105\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yes there is actually a natural function you're describing, I looked into this a lot before. But it's kind of one of those pick your poison things</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Does it exist in Mathlib?</p>",
