    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I just don't understand the premise of this question. What in your view is <code>predAbove n n</code> supposed to be?</p>",
        "id": 584287174,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1775671925
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110038\">Kevin Buzzard</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/succAbove.20and.20predAbove.20lemmas/near/584275212\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If p is <code>Fin.last n</code> then it's <code>n</code> so <code>p &lt; i</code> is never true so you want to map <code>n : Fin (n + 1)</code> to <code>n : Fin n</code> which doesn't look right in this context.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Sorry, I didn't state my concern accurately. What I found a need for is this function:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">predAbove_of_ne</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">by_cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">omega</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">omega</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It's useful if you have something for <code>k</code> and you want to extend it to all other <code>i</code> (for example, I was working with extending an independent set to an orthonormal basis).</p>",
        "id": 584287433,
        "sender_full_name": "Bjørn Kjos-Hanssen",
        "timestamp": 1775671995
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah that's the one.</p>",
        "id": 584287488,
        "sender_full_name": "Wrenna Robson",
        "timestamp": 1775672011
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I had a PR ages back calling it succAboveOfNe, but for various reasons I never got it merged</p>",
        "id": 584287561,
        "sender_full_name": "Wrenna Robson",
        "timestamp": 1775672032
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But it does naturally occur.</p>",
        "id": 584287576,
        "sender_full_name": "Wrenna Robson",
        "timestamp": 1775672037
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sorry I mean predAboveOfNe</p>",
        "id": 584287656,
        "sender_full_name": "Wrenna Robson",
        "timestamp": 1775672064
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Arguably it is the better generalisation of pred and castPred (which are in a sense its end points).</p>",
        "id": 584287727,
        "sender_full_name": "Wrenna Robson",
        "timestamp": 1775672088
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Good to know, I won't try to make a PR for it then :)</p>",
        "id": 584288138,
        "sender_full_name": "Bjørn Kjos-Hanssen",
        "timestamp": 1775672214
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh I mean I think we should have it. I just needed to get on with other stuff like getting my PhD</p>",
        "id": 584288225,
        "sender_full_name": "Wrenna Robson",
        "timestamp": 1775672240
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This may be a better version(?):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">predAbove_of_ne'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">by_cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">omega</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">omega</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This way, given <code>i : Fin m</code>, we don't have to convert <code>m</code> into <code>n.succ</code> in order to apply the definition.</p>",
        "id": 584515255,
        "sender_full_name": "Bjørn Kjos-Hanssen",
        "timestamp": 1775759011
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I would use <code>if</code> (in term mode) not <code>by_cases</code> because you're making data not proving theorems.</p>",
        "id": 584517022,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1775759715
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Fin (n -1) is sometimes an annoying shape for things to be.</p>",
        "id": 584518313,
        "sender_full_name": "Wrenna Robson",
        "timestamp": 1775760216
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Please bear in mind that Fin.predAbove is used to define the degeneracy maps in the simplex category; quite a few things depend on this. I would advise against changing its shape.</p>",
        "id": 584519732,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Carlier",
        "timestamp": 1775760742
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes you really do not want to do that - different name needed ideally if you are interested in this.</p>",
        "id": 584519866,
        "sender_full_name": "Wrenna Robson",
        "timestamp": 1775760797
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Right, the name would be <code>Fin.predAbove_of_ne</code> or something like that.</p>",
        "id": 584520318,
        "sender_full_name": "Bjørn Kjos-Hanssen",
        "timestamp": 1775760989
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think without underscores in a name but yes</p>",
        "id": 584520371,
        "sender_full_name": "Wrenna Robson",
        "timestamp": 1775761008
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's a little annoying because pred and castPred don't have conditions in their names - clearly we could define pred and castPred analogously to predAbove but that would be different. I think of one of these maps as \"the natural (order preserving) inverse to succAbove\" (in that succAbove injects to everywhere except a pivot, and predAboveOfNe inverts that as long as you aren't at the pivot), whereas predAbove is more like you've got a map that is minimally non-injective (there's one point of overlap), order preserving, and you're saying where the overlap point is in the image.</p>",
        "id": 584520877,
        "sender_full_name": "Wrenna Robson",
        "timestamp": 1775761200
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And you can very naturally define predAbove in terms of predAboveOfNe (which in theory would be fine as long as the definition being unpacked isn't used for theorems, haha).</p>",
        "id": 584520987,
        "sender_full_name": "Wrenna Robson",
        "timestamp": 1775761239
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"330967\">Wrenna Robson</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/succAbove.20and.20predAbove.20lemmas/near/584520987\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>And you can very naturally define predAbove in terms of predAboveOfNe (which in theory would be fine as long as the definition being unpacked isn't used for theorems, haha).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>As long as <code>predAbove</code> remains functionally the same map, I suppose it wouldn't matter much if there is one more layer of unpacking(?) (and maybe that's what you're saying too).</p>",
        "id": 584532647,
        "sender_full_name": "Bjørn Kjos-Hanssen",
        "timestamp": 1775765540
    }
]